{"title":"How src/tt/loca.rs Resolves Glyph IDs to glyf Byte Ranges","sections":[{"title":"Decode the loca entry into byte offsets","prose":"The file's main responsibility is implemented by `get_glyph_location`: it resolves a glyph's loca location into `GlyphLocation`, whose `offset` marks the first glyf byte and whose `length` gives the span. `index_to_loc_format` equal to zero selects short entries, while every other value takes the long branch: on the short branch, `loca` provides two big-endian 16-bit values doubled into `this` and `next`; on the long branch, two big-endian 32-bit values are used directly. For illustration, short values 3 and 5 become byte offsets 6 and 10, a four-byte candidate span.","spokenText":"A glyph lookup turns a table entry into a byte range. Zero selects the short form, while every other setting uses the long form; the short form doubles its values, while the long form already stores byte offsets. For example, three and five become six and ten.","claims":[{"category":"codeBehavior","aspect":"responsibility","prose":"The file's main responsibility is implemented by `get_glyph_location`: it resolves a glyph's loca location into `GlyphLocation`, whose `offset` marks the first glyf byte and whose `length` gives the span.","inferenceBasis":"","identifiers":["get_glyph_location","GlyphLocation","offset","length"],"evidence":[{"path":"src/tt/loca.rs","quote":"/// Resolve a glyph's location from the 'loca' table.
///
/// `index_to_loc_format` is from the 'head' table (0 = short, 1 = long).
/// Returns `Some` with `length == 0` for the empty (space-like) glyph slot.
pub fn get_glyph_location(
    loca: &[u8],
    glyph_index: u16,
    index_to_loc_format: i16,
    glyf_len: usize,
) -> Option<GlyphLocation> {"},{"path":"src/tt/loca.rs","quote":"/// `(offset, length)` of a glyph's data inside the 'glyf' table.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct GlyphLocation {
    pub offset: u32,
    pub length: u32,
}"}],"relationshipIds":[]},{"category":"codeBehavior","aspect":"inputOutput","prose":"`index_to_loc_format` equal to zero selects short entries, while every other value takes the long branch: on the short branch, `loca` provides two big-endian 16-bit values doubled into `this` and `next`; on the long branch, two big-endian 32-bit values are used directly. For illustration, short values 3 and 5 become byte offsets 6 and 10, a four-byte candidate span.","inferenceBasis":"","identifiers":["index_to_loc_format","loca","this","next"],"evidence":[{"path":"src/tt/loca.rs","quote":"/// `index_to_loc_format` is from the 'head' table (0 = short, 1 = long)."},{"path":"src/tt/loca.rs","quote":"    let (this, mut next, num_locations) = if index_to_loc_format == 0 {
        let off = idx * 2;
        let record = loca.get(off..off + 4)?;
        let this = u16::from_be_bytes([record[0], record[1]]) as u32 * 2;
        let next = u16::from_be_bytes([record[2], record[3]]) as u32 * 2;
        (this, next, loca.len() / 2)
    } else {
        let off = idx * 4;
        let record = loca.get(off..off + 8)?;
        let this = u32::from_be_bytes([record[0], record[1], record[2], record[3]]);
        let next = u32::from_be_bytes([record[4], record[5], record[6], record[7]]);
        (this, next, loca.len() / 4)
    };"}],"relationshipIds":[]}],"visual":{"kind":"dataFlow","title":"Entry formats produce byte offsets","direction":"leftToRight","nodes":[{"label":"GlyphLocation","detail":"offset and length describe the glyf byte range","evidence":[{"claimIndex":0,"evidenceIndex":1}]},{"label":"Short entries","detail":"16-bit values are doubled into byte offsets","evidence":[{"claimIndex":1,"evidenceIndex":1}]},{"label":"Long entries","detail":"32-bit values are used directly","evidence":[{"claimIndex":1,"evidenceIndex":1}]},{"label":"Candidate byte offsets","detail":"this and next","evidence":[{"claimIndex":1,"evidenceIndex":1}]}],"edges":[{"fromNodeIndex":1,"toNodeIndex":3,"label":"double the values","evidence":[{"claimIndex":1,"evidenceIndex":1}]},{"fromNodeIndex":2,"toNodeIndex":3,"label":"use directly","evidence":[{"claimIndex":1,"evidenceIndex":1}]}],"presentation":{"schemaVersion":2,"scenes":[{"claimIndex":0,"title":"The returned range record","mode":"composition","elements":[{"kind":"panel","parentIndex":null,"nodeIndex":null,"tone":"neutral","value":"","valueOrigin":"none"},{"kind":"row","parentIndex":0,"nodeIndex":null,"tone":"neutral","value":"","valueOrigin":"none"},{"kind":"card","parentIndex":1,"nodeIndex":0,"tone":"accent","value":"","valueOrigin":"none"},{"kind":"metric","parentIndex":1,"nodeIndex":0,"tone":"neutral","value":"offset","valueOrigin":"source"},{"kind":"metric","parentIndex":1,"nodeIndex":0,"tone":"neutral","value":"length","valueOrigin":"source"}]},{"claimIndex":1,"title":"Short and long offset encodings","mode":"composition","elements":[{"kind":"compare","parentIndex":null,"nodeIndex":null,"tone":"neutral","value":"","valueOrigin":"none"},{"kind":"card","parentIndex":0,"nodeIndex":1,"tone":"accent","value":"","valueOrigin":"none"},{"kind":"token","parentIndex":1,"nodeIndex":1,"tone":"positive","value":"Example: 3, 5 → 6, 10","valueOrigin":"illustration"},{"kind":"card","parentIndex":0,"nodeIndex":2,"tone":"neutral","value":"","valueOrigin":"none"},{"kind":"token","parentIndex":3,"nodeIndex":3,"tone":"neutral","value":"this, next","valueOrigin":"source"}]}]}}},{"title":"Missing records and the glyf bound","prose":"After `get_glyph_location` casts `glyph_index` to `idx`, a short lookup demands a four-byte slice from `loca` and a long lookup demands eight bytes; if either slice is missing, `?` propagates `None` from the optional result rather than returning a partial range. The supplied `glyf_len` is converted to the 32-bit offset width; if it cannot fit, comparison uses the maximum representable 32-bit value rather than returning an error.","spokenText":"The lookup asks for the bytes required by the selected format, and a missing slice produces no location. The table length is converted to the offsets' width, with the largest representable bound used if it cannot fit.","claims":[{"category":"codeBehavior","aspect":"failurePath","prose":"After `get_glyph_location` casts `glyph_index` to `idx`, a short lookup demands a four-byte slice from `loca` and a long lookup demands eight bytes; if either slice is missing, `?` propagates `None` from the optional result rather than returning a partial range.","inferenceBasis":"","identifiers":["get_glyph_location","glyph_index","idx","loca"],"evidence":[{"path":"src/tt/loca.rs","quote":"pub fn get_glyph_location(
