    let idx = glyph_index as usize;"},{"path":"src/tt/loca.rs","quote":"        let record = loca.get(off..off + 4)?;"},{"path":"src/tt/loca.rs","quote":"        let record = loca.get(off..off + 8)?;"}],"relationshipIds":[]},{"category":"codeBehavior","aspect":"inputOutput","prose":"The supplied `glyf_len` is converted to the 32-bit offset width; if it cannot fit, comparison uses the maximum representable 32-bit value rather than returning an error.","inferenceBasis":"","identifiers":["glyf_len"],"evidence":[{"path":"src/tt/loca.rs","quote":"    let glyf_len = u32::try_from(glyf_len).unwrap_or(u32::MAX);"}],"relationshipIds":[]}],"visual":{"kind":"dataFlow","title":"Record availability and table-length conversion","direction":"leftToRight","nodes":[{"label":"Short lookup","detail":"requests a four-byte entry","evidence":[{"claimIndex":0,"evidenceIndex":1}]},{"label":"Long lookup","detail":"requests an eight-byte entry","evidence":[{"claimIndex":0,"evidenceIndex":2}]},{"label":"No location","detail":"a missing slice propagates None","evidence":[{"claimIndex":0,"evidenceIndex":0},{"claimIndex":0,"evidenceIndex":1},{"claimIndex":0,"evidenceIndex":2}]},{"label":"glyf_len input","detail":"table length before offset-width conversion","evidence":[{"claimIndex":1,"evidenceIndex":0}]},{"label":"32-bit bound","detail":"converted value used for comparisons","evidence":[{"claimIndex":1,"evidenceIndex":0}]},{"label":"Maximum fallback","detail":"used when conversion cannot fit","evidence":[{"claimIndex":1,"evidenceIndex":0}]}],"edges":[{"fromNodeIndex":0,"toNodeIndex":2,"label":"if four bytes are unavailable","evidence":[{"claimIndex":0,"evidenceIndex":1}]},{"fromNodeIndex":1,"toNodeIndex":2,"label":"if eight bytes are unavailable","evidence":[{"claimIndex":0,"evidenceIndex":2}]},{"fromNodeIndex":3,"toNodeIndex":4,"label":"convert to offset width","evidence":[{"claimIndex":1,"evidenceIndex":0}]},{"fromNodeIndex":4,"toNodeIndex":5,"label":"fallback if conversion fails","evidence":[{"claimIndex":1,"evidenceIndex":0}]}],"presentation":{"schemaVersion":2,"scenes":[{"claimIndex":0,"title":"Either encoding can lack a complete entry","mode":"composition","elements":[{"kind":"compare","parentIndex":null,"nodeIndex":null,"tone":"neutral","value":"","valueOrigin":"none"},{"kind":"card","parentIndex":0,"nodeIndex":0,"tone":"accent","value":"","valueOrigin":"none"},{"kind":"card","parentIndex":0,"nodeIndex":1,"tone":"neutral","value":"","valueOrigin":"none"},{"kind":"card","parentIndex":0,"nodeIndex":2,"tone":"warning","value":"","valueOrigin":"none"}]},{"claimIndex":1,"title":"Convert the table length before checking offsets","mode":"composition","elements":[{"kind":"row","parentIndex":null,"nodeIndex":null,"tone":"neutral","value":"","valueOrigin":"none"},{"kind":"card","parentIndex":0,"nodeIndex":3,"tone":"neutral","value":"","valueOrigin":"none"},{"kind":"card","parentIndex":0,"nodeIndex":4,"tone":"accent","value":"","valueOrigin":"none"},{"kind":"card","parentIndex":0,"nodeIndex":5,"tone":"warning","value":"","valueOrigin":"none"}]}]}}},{"title":"Bounds guards and glyph length","prose":"When `this` is strictly greater than `glyf_len`, the function returns `Some` containing a `GlyphLocation` with zero `offset` and zero `length`; equality does not enter this empty-slot guard. If `next` exceeds `glyf_len`, the code changes its local `next` to the bound only when `idx` equals `num_locations.saturating_sub(2)`; every other index returns a zero-offset, zero-length location. Once the guards permit a location, `length` is `next - this` when `next` is at least `this`; for an unordered pair with `next` below `this`, it instead uses the remaining `glyf_len - this` bytes. For example, if the checks reach this calculation with `this = 20`, `next = 16`, and `glyf_len = 30`, the returned length is 10.","spokenText":"An offset already beyond the glyf data produces an empty slot. An oversized next offset is clipped only for the final-entry test; otherwise it also gives an empty slot. For a surviving pair, the code measures forward when ordered and uses the remaining table bytes when the offsets are reversed.","claims":[{"category":"codeBehavior","aspect":"failurePath","prose":"When `this` is strictly greater than `glyf_len`, the function returns `Some` containing a `GlyphLocation` with zero `offset` and zero `length`; equality does not enter this empty-slot guard.","inferenceBasis":"","identifiers":["this","glyf_len","GlyphLocation","offset","length"],"evidence":[{"path":"src/tt/loca.rs","quote":"    if this > glyf_len {
        return Some(GlyphLocation {
            offset: 0,
            length: 0,
        });
    }"}],"relationshipIds":[]},{"category":"codeBehavior","aspect":"stateEffect","prose":"If `next` exceeds `glyf_len`, the code changes its local `next` to the bound only when `idx` equals `num_locations.saturating_sub(2)`; every other index returns a zero-offset, zero-length location.","inferenceBasis":"","identifiers":["next","glyf_len","idx","num_locations"],"evidence":[{"path":"src/tt/loca.rs","quote":"    if next > glyf_len {
        if idx == num_locations.saturating_sub(2) {
            next = glyf_len;
        } else {
            return Some(GlyphLocation {
                offset: 0,
                length: 0,
            });
        }
    }"}],"relationshipIds":[]},{"category":"codeBehavior","aspect":"inputOutput","prose":"Once the guards permit a location, `length` is `next - this` when `next` is at least `this`; for an unordered pair with `next` below `this`, it instead uses the remaining `glyf_len - this` bytes. For example, if the checks reach this calculation with `this = 20`, `next = 16`, and `glyf_len = 30`, the returned length is 10.","inferenceBasis":"","identifiers":["next","this","length","glyf_len"],"evidence":[{"path":"src/tt/loca.rs","quote":"        // FreeType deliberately uses the remaining `glyf` bytes as an upper
        // bound for unordered `loca` entries instead of treating them empty.
        length: if next >= this {
            next - this
        } else {
            glyf_len - this
        },"}],"relationshipIds":[]}],"visual":{"kind":"dataFlow","title":"Out-of-bounds and unordered-offset outcomes","direction":"leftToRight","nodes":[{"label":"this beyond glyf_len","detail":"strictly greater than the bound","evidence":[{"claimIndex":0,"evidenceIndex":0}]},{"label":"Empty location","detail":"zero offset and zero length","evidence":[{"claimIndex":0,"evidenceIndex":0}]},{"label":"next beyond glyf_len","detail":"oversized next offset enters a special test","evidence":[{"claimIndex":1,"evidenceIndex":0}]},{"label":"Final-glyph guard","detail":"idx equals num_locations minus two with saturation","evidence":[{"claimIndex":1,"evidenceIndex":0}]},{"label":"Clipped next","detail":"local next is set to glyf_len","evidence":[{"claimIndex":1,"evidenceIndex":0}]},{"label":"Other index","detail":"returns an empty location","evidence":[{"claimIndex":1,"evidenceIndex":0}]},{"label":"Ordered pair","detail":"next is at least this","evidence":[{"claimIndex":2,"evidenceIndex":0}]},{"label":"Forward length","detail":"difference between next and this","evidence":[{"claimIndex":2,"evidenceIndex":0}]},{"label":"Reversed pair","detail":"next is below this","evidence":[{"claimIndex":2,"evidenceIndex":0}]},{"label":"Remaining table length","detail":"glyf_len minus this","evidence":[{"claimIndex":2,"evidenceIndex":0}]}],"edges":[{"fromNodeIndex":0,"toNodeIndex":1,"label":"returns empty","evidence":[{"claimIndex":0,"evidenceIndex":0}]},{"fromNodeIndex":2,"toNodeIndex":3,"label":"test final-glyph index","evidence":[{"claimIndex":1,"evidenceIndex":0}]},{"fromNodeIndex":3,"toNodeIndex":4,"label":"guard matches","evidence":[{"claimIndex":1,"evidenceIndex":0}]},{"fromNodeIndex":3,"toNodeIndex":5,"label":"otherwise","evidence":[{"claimIndex":1,"evidenceIndex":0}]},{"fromNodeIndex":6,"toNodeIndex":7,"label":"use the difference","evidence":[{"claimIndex":2,"evidenceIndex":0}]},{"fromNodeIndex":8,"toNodeIndex":9,"label":"use remaining bytes","evidence":[{"claimIndex":2,"evidenceInde